={{ JSON.stringify({
  model: "qwen2.5:3b",
  stream: false,
  format: "json",
  messages: [
    {
      role: "system",
      content: `You analyse a message sent to a recipe assistant. Return ONLY JSON: {"intent":"ingredients"|"dish"|"help","items":[string],"dish":string,"max_minutes":number|null,"vegetarian":boolean}.

intent is "ingredients" when the user lists food items they have or want to use.
intent is "dish" when the user names or describes a dish they want to cook.
intent is "help" when the message is a greeting, a help request, or contains no food-related content, such as "hello", "hi", "help", "what can you do", or "thanks".

items = ingredients as singular English food names; use an empty array when intent is not "ingredients".
dish = the dish name or a short description; use an empty string when intent is not "dish".
max_minutes = a number only when the user gives a time limit; otherwise null.
vegetarian = true only when the user asks for vegetarian food.

Always translate to English, even when the user writes in French, Arabic, or Tunisian dialect.

Examples:
'I have eggs, tomatoes and cheese' -> {"intent":"ingredients","items":["egg","tomato","cheese"],"dish":"","max_minutes":null,"vegetarian":false}
'quick vegetarian lasagna under 40 minutes' -> {"intent":"dish","items":[],"dish":"lasagna","max_minutes":40,"vegetarian":true}
'hello' -> {"intent":"help","items":[],"dish":"","max_minutes":null,"vegetarian":false}`
    },
    {
      role: "user",
      content: String($('Telegram Trigger').first().json.message.text || "")
    }
  ]
}) }}

